          "en": "Checklist"
        }
      }
    ],
    "formulaDescription": "Start with 13 base items. Add surface-notes when technicality is medium or high; recon-run when high. Add sunrise-sunset and night-kit when nightSection. Add crew-access, pacer-points and drop-bags when crewAccess. Add paper-map when no GPX. Add poles when gain/distance > 30 m/km. desktopMinutes = round(45 + 0.5×distanceKm + 0.02×gain + 30/15/0 for high/medium/low technicality + 20 if night + 15 if crew). reconRuns = 3/2/1 for high/medium/low. riskBand = high if night or high technicality or ≥12 h; moderate if medium technicality or ≥6 h; otherwise low.",
    "assumptions": [
      "The checklist is an editorial planning aid, not a substitute for the official race rules or mandatory-gear list.",
      "Desktop minutes are a rough planning estimate, not a promise that the review will take that long.",
      "Field recon runs assume accessible public trails; permit, closure and private-land rules are outside the tool.",
      "The tool does not judge whether a GPX is accurate, licensed or current; verify against the official source.",
      "Risk band is about planning complexity, not personal safety or medical risk.",
      "The checklist does not cover weather contingency, evacuation medical capability or local emergency numbers."
    ],
    "rounding": "Counts are integers. Desktop minutes are rounded to the nearest whole minute. The gain/distance ratio uses the unrounded inputs.",
    "caseRefs": [
      "case-course-recon-checklist-road-marathon",
      "case-course-recon-checklist-mountain-100",
      "case-course-recon-checklist-half-low"
    ]
  }
